#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0411-A expect=noViolation domain=SUPPDM
#note "The R-5.25 wave-3 split's discriminator, sibling side: QNAM RACEOTH repeats for subject 001 with IDVAR/IDVARVAL blank - the parent CDISC-CG0411's violation data, and the five-member tuple (USUBJID, RDOMAIN, IDVAR, IDVARVAL, QNAM) IS duplicated - but every row has RDOMAIN=DM, so the non-DM half's RDOMAIN != 'DM' conjunct is false and the sibling is SILENT. DM-parent duplicates belong to the bare id alone."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset SUPPDM class=RELATIONSHIP label="Supplemental Qualifiers for DM"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
---
S1 | DM | 001 |  |  | RACEOTH | Other race A
S1 | DM | 001 |  |  | RACEOTH | Other race B
